You have a tritan colour vision anomaly. This means the blue-sensitive cone system does not work in the usual way, so blue-yellow discrimination is reduced.\
\
Tritan defects are much less common than red-green colour vision anomalies. They can make some blues and greens, or some yellows and greys, harder to tell apart. This does not usually affect sharpness of vision, but it can still be important for colour-dependent tasks.\
\
